infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Naked T vs wrapped [T]
  desc Same inputs, different results — distribution vs atomic check
  compares
    - label Naked T — distributes
      children
        - label Naked: T extends U
          desc Runs once per union member, results unioned
        - label IsStringNaked<string | number>
          desc Resolves to boolean (true | false)
        - label Wrap<never>
          desc Resolves to never — empty union, body never runs
        - label Exclude / Extract / NonNullable
          desc Map members to never; never vanishes
    - label Wrapped [T] — atomic
      children
        - label Wrapped: [T] extends [U]
          desc Checks the union as one whole
        - label IsString<string | number>
          desc Resolves to false
        - label IsNever<never>
          desc Resolves to true
        - label Whole-type predicates
          desc Use when answering about the whole type
theme
  palette #6366f1 #f59e0b
